IMPORT prelude

-- Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- capital gains: indexation for individuals from 1 July 2027
-- (s 110-36(1A), s 114-10), the discount capital gain (ss 115-10 to 115-25) and the discount percentage (ss 115-100, 115-102),
-- the net capital gain (s 102-5, one gain), the main residence exemption (ss 118-110, 118-150), the small business maximum net
-- asset value test and basic condition (c) (ss 152-10(1)(c), (1AA), 152-15), and death (ss 128-10, 104-215, 118-60).
--
-- SEAT: the taxpayer -- an individual Australian resident who sells a home, a shareholding or an investment, or whose assets
-- pass on death ("What capital gain must I count?"). For d093 the question is the deceased's, asked by the executor: "Does my
-- death make a capital gain on this asset?"
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 267, compilation date 27 August 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 79, 2026; register id
-- C2026C00400, 12 volumes), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A05138.txt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. The cost base itself (Divs 110, 112) and the indexation factor (Subdiv 960-M, CPI figures published by the
-- Australian Statistician -- passed in as a factor); the deemed sale and reacquisition on 1 July 2027 of assets held on 30 June
-- 2027 (Subdiv 112-E) and the deferred gain from it; the ordering of capital losses (s 102-5 Steps 1-4); the foreign and
-- temporary resident percentages (ss 115-105 to 115-120) and affordable housing (s 115-125); partial main residence exemptions
-- (ss 118-185 to 118-192), the absence rule (s 118-145), deceased estates (s 118-195); the active asset test, s 152-10(2) for
-- shares and the concessions themselves (Subdivs 152-B to 152-E); what "net value" includes (s 152-20); beneficiaries' cost
-- bases (s 128-15). Dates are written YYYYMMDD; "12 months" is read as the same day a year later (the encoder's reading).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No
-- pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 -- capital gains`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

-- s 115-10: a discount capital gain is made by "(a) an individual; or (b) a *complying superannuation entity; or (c) a trust; or
-- (d) a *life insurance company" (complying superannuation assets only, not modelled). A company cannot make one.
DECLARE Entity IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a complying superannuation entity`
    `a trust`
    `a company`

GIVEN `who` IS AN Entity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `can make a discount capital gain` IF
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `a company` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `who` IS AN Entity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an individual or a trust` IF
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `an individual` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a trust` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `110-36(1A), 114-10 -- indexation from 1 July 2027`

-- s 110-36(1A): "The cost base of a *CGT asset also includes indexation of the elements of the cost base (except the third
-- element) for the purposes of working out the *capital gain of an individual or a trust from a *CGT event happening in relation
-- to the CGT asset if: (a) the CGT event happens on or after 1 July 2027; and (b) the requirements of Division 114 are met."
-- Note 1: it "does not extend to foreign residents or temporary residents (see section 114-25)".
-- s 114-10(1): "You only index expenditure ... if you ... had *acquired the asset at least 12 months before the time of the CGT
-- event."
@export Is the cost base of my asset indexed for a CGT event on or after 1 July 2027 (s 110-36(1A))?
GIVEN `who` IS AN Entity @desc Who makes the gain
      `foreign or temporary resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a foreign resident or a temporary resident
      `acquired on` IS A NUMBER @desc When you acquired the asset (YYYYMMDD)
      `event on` IS A NUMBER @desc When the CGT event happens (YYYYMMDD)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my cost base indexed` IF
        `is an individual or a trust` `who`
    AND NOT `foreign or temporary resident`
    AND `event on` AT LEAST 20270701
    AND `acquired on` PLUS 10000 AT MOST `event on`

-- s 104-10(4) (CGT event A1, a disposal): "You make a capital gain if the *capital proceeds from the disposal are more than
-- the asset's *cost base." With indexation the cost base
-- (except the third element) is multiplied by the indexation factor (Subdiv 960-M), which is passed in; 1 means no indexation.
-- Simplified: the whole cost base is indexed and no element is excluded.
@export What is my capital gain on this asset (capital proceeds less the cost base, indexed where s 110-36(1A) applies)?
GIVEN `who` IS AN Entity @desc Who makes the gain
      `foreign or temporary resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a foreign resident or a temporary resident
      `acquired on` IS A NUMBER @desc When you acquired the asset (YYYYMMDD)
      `event on` IS A NUMBER @desc When the CGT event happens (YYYYMMDD)
      `capital proceeds` IS A NUMBER @desc What you receive for the asset, in dollars
      `cost base` IS A NUMBER @desc The cost base before indexation, in dollars
      `indexation factor` IS A NUMBER @desc The indexation factor for the period under Subdivision 960-M (for example 1.5)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my capital gain` MEANS
    `the greater of`
        (`capital proceeds` MINUS
            (IF `Is my cost base indexed` `who` `foreign or temporary resident` `acquired on` `event on`
             THEN `cost base` TIMES `indexation factor`
             ELSE `cost base`))
        0

§§ `115-5 to 115-25 -- is it a discount capital gain`

-- s 115-15: from a CGT event after 11.45 am on 21 September 1999. s 115-20: cost base "calculated without reference to
-- indexation at any time". s 115-25(1): from a CGT event happening to a CGT asset "*acquired by the entity making the capital
-- gain at least 12 months before the CGT event".
@export Is my capital gain a discount capital gain (ss 115-10 to 115-25)?
GIVEN `who` IS AN Entity @desc Who makes the gain
      `acquired on` IS A NUMBER @desc When you acquired the asset (YYYYMMDD)
      `event on` IS A NUMBER @desc When the CGT event happens (YYYYMMDD)
      `cost base indexed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cost base was worked out with indexation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my gain a discount capital gain` IF
        `can make a discount capital gain` `who`
    AND `event on` GREATER THAN 19990921
    AND (NOT `cost base indexed`)
    AND `acquired on` PLUS 10000 AT MOST `event on`

§§ `115-100, 115-102 -- the discount percentage`

-- s 115-100: "(a) 50% if section 115-102 (about new residential dwellings) applies to the gain; or (aa) 50% if: (i) the gain is
-- made by an individual from a *CGT event happening before 1 July 2027; and (ii) neither section 115-105 nor 115-110 (about
-- foreign or temporary residents) applies ...; (ab) 50% if ... made by a trust (other than a ... complying superannuation entity)
-- from a *CGT event happening before 1 July 2027 ...; (b) 33 1/3% if the gain is made ... by a complying superannuation entity
-- ...; ... (f) 0% if none of the above paragraphs applies to the gain."
-- s 115-102(1): an individual, from a CGT event "on or after 1 July 2027 in relation to a *CGT asset covered by subsection (2)"
-- -- "a *new residential dwelling"; (5) the individual may choose for it not to apply (and index instead).
-- Foreign and temporary residents are outside this encoding: the individual is taken to be neither.
@export What is the discount percentage on my discount capital gain (ss 115-100, 115-102)?
GIVEN `who` IS AN Entity @desc Who makes the gain
      `event on` IS A NUMBER @desc When the CGT event happens (YYYYMMDD)
      `a new residential dwelling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the asset is a new residential dwelling under s 115-102(2)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my discount percentage` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `an individual` THEN (IF `event on` LESS THAN 20270701 OR `a new residential dwelling` THEN 50 ELSE 0)
    WHEN `a trust` THEN (IF `event on` LESS THAN 20270701 THEN 50 ELSE 0)
    WHEN `a complying superannuation entity` THEN 100 DIVIDED BY 3
    OTHERWISE 0

§§ `102-5 -- net capital gain (one gain)`

-- s 102-5(1): Step 1 reduce capital gains by capital losses; Step 2 apply earlier net capital losses; Step 5 "Reduce by the
-- *discount percentage each amount of any *discount capital gain remaining"; Step 6 small business concessions (not encoded);
-- Step 7 the sum is the net capital gain. Simplified to a single gain with the losses applied to it.
@export What is my net capital gain from this one gain (s 102-5)?
GIVEN `capital gain` IS A NUMBER @desc The capital gain, in dollars
      `losses applied` IS A NUMBER @desc Capital losses and earlier net capital losses applied to it, in dollars
      `discount percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The discount percentage (0 if not a discount capital gain)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my net capital gain` MEANS
    (`the greater of` (`capital gain` MINUS `losses applied`) 0) TIMES (100 MINUS `discount percentage`) DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `118-110, 118-150 -- main residence`

-- s 118-110(1): a capital gain or loss from a CGT event to "a *dwelling or your *ownership interest in it is disregarded if:
-- (a) you are an individual; and (b) the dwelling was your main residence throughout your *ownership period; and (c) the
-- interest did not *pass to you as a beneficiary in, and you did not *acquire it as a trustee of, the estate of a deceased
-- person." (3) "However, this section does not apply if, at the time the *CGT event happens, you: (a) are an *excluded foreign
-- resident; or (b) are a foreign resident who does not satisfy the *life events test."
-- s 118-150: if you build a dwelling on land you own, "(2) You can choose to apply this Subdivision as if the *dwelling ... were
-- your main residence from the time you *acquired the *ownership interest"; (3) only if it becomes your main residence "as soon
-- as practicable after the work is finished" and continues so "for at least 3 months"; (4) for at most 4 years before it
-- becomes your main residence. The Commissioner's longer time is not modelled.
DECLARE DwellingSale HAS
    `main residence from acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months from acquisition before it became the main residence` IS A NUMBER
    `main residence from then until the sale` IS A BOOLEAN
    `built on the land and moved in as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lived in for at least 3 months` IS A BOOLEAN
    `chooses section 118-150` IS A BOOLEAN
    `inherited or held as trustee of an estate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `excluded foreign resident or failing the life events test` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the sale` IS A DwellingSale
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the building choice covers the gap` IF
        `the sale`'s `chooses section 118-150`
    AND `the sale`'s `built on the land and moved in as soon as practicable`
    AND `the sale`'s `lived in for at least 3 months`
    AND `the sale`'s `months from acquisition before it became the main residence` AT MOST 48

@export Is the capital gain on my home disregarded as my main residence (ss 118-110, 118-150)?
GIVEN `the sale` IS A DwellingSale @desc The home you sold and how you lived in it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the gain on my home disregarded` IF
        (`the sale`'s `main residence from acquisition` OR (`the sale`'s `main residence from then until the sale` AND `the building choice covers the gap` `the sale`))
    AND (NOT `the sale`'s `inherited or held as trustee of an estate`)
    AND (NOT `the sale`'s `excluded foreign resident or failing the life events test`)

§§ `152-10(1)(c), (1AA), 152-15 -- small business: can I get relief`

-- s 152-10(1)(c): "at least one of the following applies: (i) you are a *CGT small business entity for the income year; (ii) you
-- satisfy the maximum net asset value test (see section 152-15); ..." (iii)-(iv) partnership and passive-asset routes, one fact.
-- (1AA): a CGT small business entity is a small business entity that would still be one "if each reference in section 328-110
-- to $10 million were a reference to $2 million".
-- s 152-15: "You satisfy the maximum net asset value test if, just before the *CGT event, the sum of the following amounts does
-- not exceed $6,000,000: (a) the *net value of the CGT assets of yours; (b) ... of any entities *connected with you; (c) ... of any
-- *affiliates of yours". Condition (c) is one of several; meeting it does not by itself give any concession.
@export Do I meet basic condition (c) for the small business CGT concessions (ss 152-10(1)(c), 152-15)?
GIVEN `carries on a business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you carry on a business yourself
      `aggregated turnover` IS A NUMBER @desc Your aggregated turnover for the income year, in dollars
      `net value of yours, connected entities and affiliates` IS A NUMBER @desc Just before the CGT event, the net value of the CGT assets of you, your connected entities and your affiliates, in dollars
      `partnership or passive asset route` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether s 152-10(1)(c)(iii) or (iv) applies to you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I meet basic condition (c)` IF
        (`carries on a business` AND `aggregated turnover` LESS THAN 2000000)
    OR  `net value of yours, connected entities and affiliates` AT MOST 6000000
    OR  `partnership or passive asset route`

§§ `128-10, 104-215, 118-60 -- death`

-- s 128-10: "When you die, a *capital gain or *capital loss from a *CGT event that results for a *CGT asset you owned just before
-- dying is disregarded." s 104-215: CGT event K3 happens if the asset passes to a beneficiary who "(a) is an *exempt entity; or
-- (b) is the trustee of a *complying superannuation entity; or (c) is a foreign resident" ((2): for a foreign resident only where
-- the asset is not *taxable Australian property); (5) disregarded if acquired "before 20 September 1985".
-- s 118-60(1): "A *capital gain or *capital loss made from a testamentary gift of property that would have been deductible under
-- section 30-15 if it had not been a testamentary gift is disregarded."
DECLARE Beneficiary IS ONE OF
    `an Australian resident individual or ordinary trust`
    `an exempt entity`
    `the trustee of a complying superannuation entity`
    `a foreign resident, the asset not taxable Australian property`
    `a foreign resident, the asset taxable Australian property`

GIVEN `beneficiary` IS A Beneficiary
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `CGT event K3 would happen` IF
    CONSIDER `beneficiary`
    WHEN `an exempt entity` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the trustee of a complying superannuation entity` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a foreign resident, the asset not taxable Australian property` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@export Does my death make a capital gain on an asset that passes under my will (ss 128-10, 104-215, 118-60)?
GIVEN `beneficiary` IS A Beneficiary @desc Who the asset passes to
      `acquired on` IS A NUMBER @desc When you acquired the asset (YYYYMMDD)
      `would be a deductible gift but for being testamentary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a gift by will that s 30-15 would allow but for s 30-15(2)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my death make a capital gain` IF
        `CGT event K3 would happen` `beneficiary`
    AND `acquired on` AT LEAST 19850920
    AND (NOT `would be a deductible gift but for being testamentary`)
